WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.400
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.133
Hey, you made it.
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:11.434
Well, guys, a search for a new
Supreme Court justice has begun.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:15.167
Today, it was announced that the
oldest justice on the bench,

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:18.200
Stephen Breyer, is retiring.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.701
Yep, at 83,
Breyer only has two options --

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.367
either retire
or play quarterback

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:23.667
for the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:27.200
[ Laughter ]
That's the only thing he's got.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.100
Yep, Breyer said he wants to
retire so he can spend more time

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.133
looking like a wise shopkeeper
from a Hallmark Christmas movie.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.834
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.334
-Yeah, it was clear Breyer's
been thinking about this.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.601
During the last case,
the only question he asked was,

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.200
"When's nap time?"

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.334
That's right,
Breyer is retiring at 83.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:49.133
Meanwhile, House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi just announced

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:53.334
she's seeking re-election
despite turning 82 in March.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:54.667
And now other members
of the House

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.601
are speaking out
about her decision.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.968
For example,
Congressman Don Young said...

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:06.801
-Really?

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.234
-Next up,
Congressman French Hill said...

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.801
Then Congresswoman Lucy McBath
said...

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.100
Then Congressman Susan Wild
said...

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.634
And Congressman Ted Budd said...

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.400
Congressman Barry Moore said...

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.634
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:58.534
♪♪

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.934
[ Applause ]

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.100
-And, finally,
Congressman Neal Dunn said...

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:09.100
[ Laughter and applause ]
Everyone had something to say.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.968
At least --
Everyone's very vocal.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:15.367
Speaking of Congress,
a bipartisan group of Senators

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.734
just announced legislation
to make the U.S.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.367
more prepared for a pandemic.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.067
Wow, great timing.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.667
Next week, they're gonna come up
with a plan to fight this

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.901
Y2K thing I keep hearing about.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.901
And listen to this --
Rudy Giuliani was asked

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:34.601
to turn over files for an
election lawsuit against him,

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:35.968
but he said that he can't

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.667
because the FBI
seized all of his computers.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:41.901
I'm no legal expert, but...

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.467
[ As Jeff Foxworthy ]
..."if all your evidence

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:48.100
from one investigation
is being used in another,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.767
you might be going to jail."

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:56.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:57.801
[ Normal voice ]
Hey, this is cool.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.767
Yesterday,
David Ortiz was elected

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.801
to the baseball Hall of Fame.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.801
Big Papi.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.868
And that's not
the only good news he got.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:11.701
Check out the phone call that
Ortiz got later that same day.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:12.701
Watch this.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.501
-Hi.
I'm calling for David Ortiz.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.801
-This is David Ortiz.

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:18.267
-Hi, David.
I'm Nathan.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.267
I'm calling in regards
to your Seamless order,

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.667
the carnitas burrito
with a side of queso.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:23.968
I'd like to apologize.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.601
We're actually running
a little bit late.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.367
But in order
to make up for that,

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.234
we're throwing in free chips
and guac for you.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:31.200
-Yes!
[ Cheering ]

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.334
That's right.
Congratulations, Mr. Ortiz.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:37.634
-Amazing.
-Free?

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.667
Wow.
-And guac?

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.133
-Yeah.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.334
And, finally,
this is going viral on TikTok.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.033
A police officer in South Dakota

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.801
showed up at a woman's door
for a pretty unusual reason.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.033
Take a look at this video.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:54.667
[ Doorbell ringing ]

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.200
-I know I'm not
who you're expecting, but...

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.567
-Hi.
-Your driver got arrested for

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.467
warrants he didn't take care of.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:03.567
So, I figured
I'd complete the DoorDash.

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.234
-[ Laughing ]
Thank you so much!

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.901
-Take care.
-Thanks!

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:09.133
-Come on.
-Come on.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.834
[ Applause ]

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.000
He's a good man.
That's right.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.000
The officer delivered
her DoorDash order

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.434
while an Uber Eats guy
took the driver to jail.

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:19.667
We have a great show.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.467
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen!

